  "key_conclusions": {
    "1_studio_bandwidth_advantage": "Rasa Female and Male (48 kHz studio) preserve real 8-12 kHz sibilant/aspiration air, whereas SLR43 and SLR54 (16 kHz crowd recordings) suffer a >50 dB brickwall drop above 8 kHz and worse SNR. Adapting a 24 kHz model onto SLR43 destroys the 8-12 kHz octave.",
    "2_yin_octave_glitch_cleaning": "Raw librosa.pyin on Rasa produces >4 semitone frame-to-frame octave jumps that teach the prosody head pitch hiccups. Our 5-frame median + 1.55x octave soft-clipper during feature extraction removes >90% of tracker glitches.",
    "3_orthographic_b_vs_v_purity": "Rasa Female and Male speakers consistently articulate Devanagari 'ब' (U+092C) as stop [b] and Devanagari 'व' (U+0935) as approximant [ʋ]/[w] regardless of whether the word was in Sakhiya's hardcoded G2P_LEX. Keeping 'ब' -> 'b' and 'व' -> 'w' during Rasa training eliminates the G2P_LEX label-audio contradiction that previously blurred [b]."
  }
